        },
        "intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>I'm Tom Bannerman, an aerospace engineer on the Gold Coast. I love technology, creativity and the water — which is why so much of this work is underwater.</p><p>I shoot digital below the surface and 35mm film above it. Every print buys more time in the water and more film through the camera.</p>"
          }
        },
        "earth_label": {
          "type": "caption",
          "settings": {
            "caption": "EARTH collection",
            "text_style": "caption-with-letter-spacing",
            "text_size": "medium"
          }
        },
        "earth_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>In the ocean the encounters are brief. Often it's a single moment where it's possible to capture the true magnificence of Mother Earth's beauty — one pass, one turn of the light. Most of the time you miss it. The EARTH collection is the frames I didn't: my best work, and the ones worth printing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "travel_label": {
          "type": "caption",
          "settings": {
            "caption": "TRAVEL collection",
            "text_style": "caption-with-letter-spacing",
            "text_size": "medium"
          }
        },
        "travel_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>An assortment of 35mm film photographs captured while backpacking around the globe. Shot slowly, on a limited number of frames, in places I'll likely never stand again.</p>"
          }
        },
        "button": {
          "type": "button",
